    {
      "id": "NS1",
      "text": "**Scenario 1 (Parity split):** GitHub INTENTS documents asset ingest and Azure INTENTS does not (or the reverse). `test-provider-parity.js` fails (violates AC1, AC19, AC20).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS2",
      "text": "**Scenario 2 (New intent leak):** A `fetch-assets` (or similar) heading/table row exists on only one SCM without an allowlist row. Parity test fails (violates AC1).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS3",
      "text": "**Scenario 3 (Silent host switch):** ADO PAT missing causes the agent to run GitHub download instead of STOP. Violates AC8 and contract shared rule 3.",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS4",
      "text": "**Scenario 4 (Stripped ADO images):** Description HTML contains `<img src=\"…/_apis/wit/attachments/…\">` and `clean_html` drops the src so ingest finds nothing. Fixture test fails (violates AC3, AC23).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS5",
      "text": "**Scenario 5 (Remote leftover):** Spec of record still points at `user-images.githubusercontent.com` or an ADO attachment URL after a successful `ok` download. Fixture test fails (violates AC12).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS6",
      "text": "**Scenario 6 (Hard fail on one 404):** A single missing attachment exits the converter non-zero and skips spec write. Fixture test fails (violates AC11).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS7",
      "text": "**Scenario 7 (Disallowed host):** Markdown image points at an arbitrary `https://example.com/x.png` and the helper downloads it. Fixture test fails (violates AC9).",
      "tests": [],
      "linkEventIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NS8",
      "text": "**Scenario 8 (Plan-only assets):** Files exist only under `{us-dir}/attachments/` and `{specsDir}/{specStem}.assets/` is missing, so `ws-cleanup` of the plan dir loses templates. Violates AC5, AC27.",
      "tests": [],
